SEVERITY CLASSIFICATION MODEL
TSPI-AI classifies all individuals into four biological network states.
Level 0 Preventive Longevity & Network Optimization Stage
Level 1 Functional Imbalance Stage
Level 2 Systemic Dysfunction Stage
Level 3 Advanced Network Failure Stage

LEVEL 0
Preventive Longevity & Network Optimization Stage
Definition
A proactive optimization stage designed for healthy individuals, longevity-focused individuals, executives, athletes, wellness clients, and individuals seeking to maximize biological performance and healthy aging.
This level is not intended for disease treatment.
Its objective is to maintain Prakati, enhance resilience, delay biological aging, and prevent future network deterioration.

Core Philosophy
The goal is not merely preventing disease.
The goal is to optimize biological networks before dysfunction occurs.

Characteristics
Healthy individuals
No significant symptoms
Normal daily function
No active disease
Minimal inflammatory burden
Stable laboratory markers
High adaptive capacity

