LEVEL 3
Advanced Network Failure Stage
Definition
A state of severe biological network dysregulation characterized by excessive inflammatory signaling, progressive tissue injury, impaired adaptive capacity and accelerated biological decline.
Level 3 is defined primarily by network activity rather than disease name.
A patient may enter Level 3 despite not having terminal disease whenever inflammatory signaling becomes sufficiently intense to drive disease progression.

HIGH INFLAMMATORY SIGNAL PRINCIPLE
